NAME
       tee - copy standard input to files and to the screen at the same time

SYNOPSIS
       tee [-a] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       tee reads standard input and writes it both to standard output and to
       each FILE, like a T-shaped pipe fitting. Put it in the middle of a pipe
       to save what passes through and still see it (or pass it on).

       tee is also how a normal user writes to a root-owned file with sudo:
       in "sudo echo x > file" the redirection is done by your own shell, not
       by sudo, so it fails; "echo x | sudo tee file" works.

OPTIONS
       -a, --append
              Add to the end of the files instead of replacing them.

       -i, --ignore-interrupts
              Ignore Ctrl+C.

EXAMPLES
       Save a list and look at it at once:

           find /etc -name '*.conf' | tee /root/conf-files.txt

       Add a line to /etc/hosts as student:

           echo '192.168.50.12 server2' | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts

SEE ALSO
       cat(1), sudo(8), bash(1)
